  37: **Cross-thread consequence:** the arm thread's tip-over FEA assumes 40 mm of shell and link crush. The shell has 8 to 17 mm of gap to the
  38: frame at the back and sides (14 to 55 mm at the front). A backward fall onto the shell alone gives far less crush than assumed, so
  39: either the FEA uses ~10 mm at the back (peaks scale up about 4x) or the shell adds crush bumpers (TPU, section 6).
