  41: ## 2. Split strategy
  42: 
  43: Two kinds of seam, treated differently:
  44: 
  45: - **Print splits** exist only because a part is wider than the P2S. They are bolted, not glued, on inner splice plates, so a
  46:   cracked piece is reprinted on its own. They sit in natural grooves (sternum, spine) so they read as design lines.
  47: - **Service splits** are where a unit comes off the robot. Each service unit has one fixed interface (hardpoint holes plus two
  48:   locating pins), so colour, shape and vent variants swap without touching the frame.
  49: 
  50: Every seam gets a deliberate 1 mm V shadow gap. A designed reveal hides the A�0.3 mm a printed panel will be out, where a flush butt
  51: joint would show every error. Laps are 8 mm, with the upper or outer piece over the lower one so it sheds dust and doesn't catch.
  52: 
