  69: 
  70: **Mass and time (estimate):** 1.23 kg of PETG for the shell, 22 g support, 32 to 53 h of printing at 6 to 10 mmA3/s effective.
  71: Add about 160 g for hardpoint brackets and 60 g of fasteners and magnets: roughly **1.45 kg** on the robot. The 2.4 mm wall is
  72: the main lever: 2.0 mm saves about 200 g (coupon C7 decides). These are volume-based estimates; Bambu Studio slices replace them
  73: at stage 3.
  74: 
  75: Not yet in the pipeline: chest shield plate, splice plates, bosses, laps and ribs (all SolidWorks work).
  76: 
  77: ## 3. Join methods compared
  78: 
  79: | Method | Use | For | Against | Verdict |
  80: | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
  81: | Inner splice plate, M3 into heat-set inserts | Print splits | Strong, reversible, one piece reprints alone | Screws only from inside: assemble the unit on the bench | **Use for print splits** |
  82: | Lap + locating pins + M3 to hardpoint | Service units | Repeatable location despite print error; outside access | Visible screw heads unless hidden | **Use for units**, heads in shadow gaps, under the arm and in the socket rim |
  83: | Magnets + hinge tabs | Doors, hatches | Tool-free, fast | Can pop open in a fall | **Use for doors**, plus an optional M3 lock screw for test runs |
  84: | Printed snap clips | Abdomen bands | No hardware | PETG fatigues, breaks in a fall | Coupon C5 first; fallback is M3 |
  85: | Dovetail / sliding key | Print splits | Hidden, no hardware | Tight tolerances on curved parts, hard to reprint one side | Coupon C5 as an alternative |
  86: | Glue (CA, epoxy) | | Simple | Not swappable, one crack means the whole unit | **Rejected** |
  87: | Quarter-turn fasteners | Doors | Positive lock | Extra parts, bulk | Later option if magnets fail C6 |
  88: 
  89: ## 4. Mounting and assembly
  90: 
  91: **Hardpoints (`../concept/generator/mounts.json`, orange in `SHELL_MFG_MOUNTS.png`):** 20 printed PETG brackets on M5 T-nuts,
  92: each carrying M3 heat-set inserts. Panels carry only clearance holes and pins, so a reprinted panel needs no inserts. The panel boss
  93: is designed to tear out before the bracket does, so a crash breaks the cheap part.
  94: 
  95: | ID | On | Qty | Carries | Gap to shell, mm (with the fix) |
  96: | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
  97: | H1 | Upper box top front rail, front face | 2 | U1 top edge | 33 |
  98: | H2 | Upper box top rear rail, rear face | 2 | U2 top edge, D3 catch | 21 |
  99: | H3 | Step shared rail, front and rear faces, between the gussets (Y A�35) | 4 | U1/U2 bottom, U3/U4 top, D1 frame | 43 front, 22 rear |
 100: | H4 | Lower box bottom rails, front and rear faces | 4 | U3/U4 bottom, D2 frame | 15 front, 19 rear |
 101: | H5 | Lower box corner posts, outer side faces | 4 | U3/U4 sides, V1 grilles | 25 to 32 |
 102: | H6 | Lower box bottom side rails, outer side faces (under-face left free for the hip interface) | 4 | Abdomen band carrier | to check |
 103: | C | Pitch RS03, 8 unused outboard M4 holes per side | 2 | Collar halves; U1/U2 socket rims lap on (location only) | 0 |
