 106: (**unresolved**: compute shelf, PDB and harness clips may already use some).
 107: 
 108: **Fasteners (estimate):** 40 A- M5A-10 + T-nuts for brackets; about 40 A- M3 heat-set inserts (M3A-5.7) with M3A-8 button heads and
 109: nylon washers; 8 A- 6A-3 mm N52 magnets per door; the existing collar M4A-10 button heads.
 110: 
 111: **Assembly order:** frame and actuators in, harness dressed �+' hardpoints �+' collars (halves) �+' U3/U4 lower units (each assembled on
 112: the bench first) �+' U1/U2 upper units �+' D1/D2 doors, D3 hatches, V1 grilles �+' abdomen carrier and bands. Every unit comes off
 113: with the arms fitted, because the collar is split and the U1/U2 seam passes through the shoulder socket.
