 128: ## 6. Cooling (estimate)
 129: 
 130: Heat in the chest: two pitch RS03s (assume 15 W each on average when holding), Pi 5 (~8 W), Jetson Orin Nano (7 to 25 W by power mode), PDB and converters (~5 W): **about 55 to 70 W**. Frame release 2477a12 adds two 40 mm exhaust fans behind D1 and one intake fan low at the front.
 131: 
 132: Chimney flow from low intakes to high exhausts, 0.3 m apart, 15 K rise: draft speed about 0.33 m/s, so natural convection needs
 133: about **75 cmA� net free area** at each end (about 150 cmA� gross with a 50% open grille).
 134: 
 135: - **Intake (low):** V1 side grilles, 2 A- ~130 cmA� gross, louvres angled down; abdomen band gaps.
 136: - **Exhaust (high):** the two 40 mm fans blow out through D1's louvres (louvre free area at least the fans' 2 A- 12.5 cmA�; fan guard 6 mm max); neck ring gap.
 137: - **Front intake fan:** needs a front grille. Frame spec 6ba6c61 puts it at torso Y 250�?"295, X A�20, fully inside U3, which gets a front grille (�% 6 mm slots) over it.
 138: - **Variants:** D1 plain, louvred, or with a 40 A- 10 mm fan (each ~2.4 L/s; two fans move ~4.8 L/s, enough for 70 W at a 12 K rise). V1 lattice
 139:   or open mesh. The swap interface stays fixed.
 140: - Slots no wider than 6 mm (fingers, cable snags). The shoulder RS03s also shed heat through their exposed output faces.
 141: - **Unresolved:** real RS03 losses at the duty cycle. Log RS03 temperatures with and without the shell in the first powered run.
 142: 
 143: Crush bumpers (TPU 95A) under the shoulder socket rims and on the lower back corners give back some of the crush distance lost in
 144: section 1, as another swappable part.
 145: 
 146: ## 7. Material and print settings (to confirm with coupons and a slice)
 147: 
 148: - **Material: PETG** (Bambu PETG HF) for panels, doors and brackets. It is tough in a fall, and holds shape near warm actuators.
 149:   PLA softens around 60 A�C and is brittle. ASA is a later option for UV and heat. TPU 95A for bumpers.
 150: - 0.4 mm High Flow nozzle (fitted), 0.2 mm layers, 6 walls (solid 2.4 mm), textured PEI plate. Bosses at 100%.
 151: - Orientation from the script (`SHELL_MFG_PLATES.png`): large panels stand on an edge so the visible face is a wall surface, with
 152:   tree supports only on the inside. Seam position: rear, aligned to the shadow-gap lines. Brim on the tall standing pieces.
 153: - A full 3MF and an exact-settings checklist come with each print release, after gate 2.
 154: 
